[phase] Contract
[delegate] architect <- Author the target-language contract in analysis/brief.md from analysis/source-map.md: define module boundaries, public API signatures, core data types, error-handling strategy, and an explicit mapping for each of the 10 gap flags (function pointers, #ifdef variants, macros, manual malloc/free, FILE*, raw byte mutation, fixed-width ints, atoi, R graphics, make/coverage flags) to target-language equivalents.
[delegate] validator <- Validate analysis/brief.md against analysis/source-map.md: confirm every one of the 10 gap flags has an explicit target-language mapping, every frozen contract (avalanche semantics, Matrix layout, HashFn contract, output format, CLI contract, reference data files) is stated unambiguously, module boundaries and public API signatures are complete and non-contradictory, and the bottom-up build order is coherent. Report any gaps, ambiguities, or contradictions as a gap list; do not rewrite the contract.
[delegate] architect <- Fix analysis/brief.md to resolve the three validator-reported contradictions: (1) align the CLI exit-code contract with source fnv_1a.c:54-56 (which returns 0 on missing input) — pick one behavior and state it explicitly, removing the non-zero-exit requirement at brief.md:56; (2) make the HashFn signature consistent — brief.md:18 includes key_len but brief.md:54 omits it — pick one canonical signature and use it everywhere; (3) correct the output-format contract at brief.md:55/57 — C "% 6.4g" emits a leading space per cell, so byte-for-byte reproduction against the single-space-delimited reference data files is unachievable; redefine the output contract to a well-defined, reproducible format (e.g., fixed-width with explicit spacing) and state exactly how it will be validated against the reference data. Keep all 10 gap-flag mappings and the 6 frozen contracts intact and non-contradictory. Do not touch source files.
