[phase] Planning
[delegate] planner <- Produce the migration batch plan in meta/plan.md from analysis/brief.md (the validated contract) and analysis/source-map.md. Partition every target module (avalanche lib, fnv_1a hash, matrix_test driver, CLI driver, build system, viz) into batches such that each module appears in exactly one batch, and order the batches so dependencies compile bottom-up (lib → fnv → drivers → build/viz). For each batch list: its modules, the source files it translates, the target files it produces, its dependencies on earlier batches, and its validation/test gate. Do not write product code and do not modify the contract.
[phase] Pilot
[delegate] translator <- Translate Batch 1 (the avalanche library crate) per meta/plan.md: produce target/src/lib.rs and target/Cargo.toml (lib target only) from source/src/avalanche.h and source/src/avalanche.c, applying the plan's gap decisions exactly — HashFn trait with fn hash(&self, key: &[u8], out: &mut [u32]); Matrix { n_rows, n_cols, vals: Vec<f64> } with new (zero-init), get, set; avalanche() taking R: Read and returning/accepting W: Write; write_to<W: Write> emitting the fixed-width 6-char, single-space-delimited, no-trailing-space format; key mutation key[i_byte] ^= 0x80u8 >> i_bit; u32/u64/usize fixed-width ints. Do not add bins, tests, or the fnv module (later batches). Ensure `cargo build` succeeds for the lib target.
[delegate] tester <- Write and run the Batch 1 (avalanche lib) characterize tests per meta/plan.md Batch 1 validation gate, in target/tests/ (add a [[test]] target to target/Cargo.toml if needed): (1) a deterministic stub HashFn (e.g. a fixed bit-mixing function with a known hash_words) run through avalanche() over a small in-memory key stream (R: Read over a Vec<u8>), asserting the resulting Matrix has rows = key_len*8, cols = hash_words*32, and each cell equals the fraction of keys whose j-th output bit flipped (compute the expected value independently in the test); (2) a write_to<W: Write> format check into a Vec<u8> asserting the fixed-width 6-char, single-space-delimited, no-trailing-space, one-\n-per-row layout. Ensure `cargo build` and `cargo test` both pass for the lib target. Do not add bins, the fnv module, or CLI drivers (later batches). Report the exact test names, the pass/fail of each, and any contract mismatch you find (report mismatches as a gap, do not rewrite the contract).
[delegate] translator <- Translate Batch 2 (the FNV-1a hash module) per meta/plan.md: produce target/src/fnv.rs from source/tests/fnv_1a.c (lines 16-50, the hash bodies only, not the main driver), applying the plan's gap decisions exactly — two distinct structs Fnv1a (1 word) and Fnv1aMulti (4 words), each implementing the HashFn trait from the avalanche lib (fn hash(&self, key: &[u8], out: &mut [u32]) and fn hash_words(&self) -> usize returning 1 or 4 respectively), using u32/u64 fixed-width ints for the FNV-1a computation. Add a `pub mod fnv;` (or equivalent) to target/src/lib.rs so the module is part of the crate. Do not add bins, CLI drivers, or matrix_test (Batch 3). Ensure `cargo build` succeeds for the lib target with fnv.rs compiled in. Report the exact struct names, the hash_words values, and the build result.
[delegate] tester <- Write and run the Batch 2 (FNV-1a) characterize tests per meta/plan.md Batch 2 validation gate, in target/tests/ (add a [[test]] target to target/Cargo.toml if needed): (1) assert Fnv1a reproduces the known FNV-1a 32-bit value for key "a" -> 0xe40c292c (compute via Fnv1a::hash into a 1-word out buffer and compare); (2) assert Fnv1aMulti reproduces the 4-word FNV-1a value for a fixed key (compute the expected 4 u32 words independently in the test using the standard FNV-1a 32-bit algorithm applied per the source's multi-word scheme, and compare all 4 words). Also assert Fnv1a::hash_words()==1 and Fnv1aMulti::hash_words()==4. Ensure `cargo build` and `cargo test` both pass. Do not add bins, CLI drivers, or matrix_test (Batch 3). Report the exact test names, pass/fail of each, and any contract mismatch (report as a gap, do not rewrite the contract).
[delegate] translator <- Translate Batch 3 (CLI drivers + matrix self-test) per meta/plan.md: produce target/src/bin/fnv_32.rs and target/src/bin/fnv_mw.rs from source/tests/fnv_1a.c (lines 51-77, the main driver only — arg parsing, fopen/fread/fprintf/fclose), and target/tests/matrix_test.rs from source/tests/matrix_test.c (test_macros, print_hilbert, main). Apply the plan's gap decisions exactly: CLI parsing via std::env::args() + arg.parse::<usize>() with defaults key_len=16, num_iter=10000 and Result/eprintln! on parse failure; FILE* streams via std::fs::File / &[u8] for input and std::io::stdout() for output; CLI contract fnv_32 <input_src> [key_len=16] [num_iter=10000] with exit 0 on success AND on missing input arg (stderr message), non-zero only on input-file open failure. fnv_32 uses Fnv1a, fnv_mw uses Fnv1aMulti, both calling avalanche() then write_to() to stdout. matrix_test.rs must: round-trip Matrix::new + set/get, and build a 3x3 Hilbert matrix via write_to into a Vec<u8> asserting the exact formatted output (fixed-width 6-char, single-space-delimited, no trailing space, one \n per row). Add [[bin]] fnv_32, [[bin]] fnv_mw, and [[test]] matrix_test to target/Cargo.toml. Do NOT add the build-system/data/README (Batch 4) or viz. Ensure `cargo build` succeeds for both bins and the test target, and `cargo test` runs matrix_test.rs green. Report the exact bin/test names, build result, and any contract mismatch (report as a gap, do not rewrite the contract).
