[delegate] repairer <- Fix the output-format defect in target/src/lib.rs: the write_to function (around line 65) currently formats each matrix cell with `{:6.4e}`, which yields 8–9 character variable-width cells (e.g. "5.0000e-1"), violating the brief's frozen contract of exactly-6-char fixed-width, single-space-delimited, no-trailing-space cells (e.g. " 0.442"). Change the cell format to a fixed-width 6-character representation (e.g. `format!("{:6.4}", value)` or an equivalent that always yields exactly 6 chars including the leading space for values < 1), keeping single-space delimiters, no trailing space, and one `\n` per row. Then update target/tests/avalanche_lib.rs (the write_to format test) and target/tests/matrix_test.rs (print_hilbert) so they assert the corrected exactly-6-char format instead of the old >=6-char behavior. Do not touch fnv.rs, the bins, the contract, or the data files. Ensure `cargo build --workspace` exits 0 and `cargo test --workspace` is fully green (all avalanche_lib, fnv_characterize, and matrix_test tests pass). Report the exact changed lines, the new format string, and the build/test results.
